    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36492" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plācāmen</span></b> ,
			ĭnis, n.
		placo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a means of pacifying</i> or <i>appeasing</i>,
				<i>a lenitive</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caelestis irae placamina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					7, 2, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">duc praedicta sacris duro placamina Diti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					13, 415</span></i>
			; cf. placamentum.</div>
